In complex simulations, multiple factors can significantly impact outcomes, 
resulting in a single optimal solution that balances all considerations. 
However, identifying this optimal solution is often hindered by the lack of 
precise information regarding these factors. To address this issue, we've 
developed a method for learning how to prioritize these factors effectively, 
utilizing available information to guide the process. Our approach is 
flexible and adaptable to various types of information, as well as different 
simulation types, and we've successfully applied it to two real-world scenarios. 
Additionally, we've demonstrated that incorporating prior knowledge can 
substantially improve results. Our method, along with the associated tools and 
information, are freely available online. 
